messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/ras/ras2tif.c
Line: 207
Function: main
Bug type: divide-by-zero
CWE: CWE-369
Explanation: rowsperstrip is computed as (8*1024)/bpsl on line 195. For images where bytes-per-scanline (bpsl) exceeds 8192 (e.g., width >= ~2731 at 24 bpp), rowsperstrip becomes 0, leading to a division by zero in height / rowsperstrip when setting TIFFTAG_STRIPBYTECOUNTS.

Source context:
```c
      167: 
      168:     switch (depth)
      169:     {
      170:         case 1:
      171:             samplesperpixel = 1;
      172:             bitspersample = 1;
      173:             photometric = PHOTOMETRIC_MINISBLACK;
      174:             break;
      175:         case 8:
      176:             samplesperpixel = 1;
      177:             bitspersample = 8;
      178:             photometric = PHOTOMETRIC_PALETTE;
      179:             break;
      180:         case 24:
      181:             samplesperpixel = 3;
      182:             bitspersample = 8;
      183:             photometric = PHOTOMETRIC_RGB;
      184:             break;
      185:         case 32:
